{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all","id":1129350,"title":"Are Exigents Yoo much of a generic catch-all?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T12:13:40-07:00","id":1129350,"title":"Are Exigents Yoo much of a generic catch-all?","content":"Does anyone else feel that Exigents could become too much of a &quot;solution&quot; for every problem? Just in my personal experience and what I see on these forums it feels like they are showing up disproportionately as NPCs and Antagonists perfectly endowed with the godly power to exactly fit the situation as it arises. I think this stems from the way they have been presented, Exigents so far have no coherent theme as a splat the way Solars, DBs, Lunars, Sidereals, or Abyssals do, they just seem to be a toolbox to do anything but are missing those narrative walls which challenge players to work within them or break them.<br /> <br /> I personally think there never should have been Exigents in the first place, to me a much more interesting area to explore would have been beefed up god-blooded and a exploration of familial expectation, inheritance, and even apotheosis, but that seems like a moot thought at this point as the gameline has committed to Exigents as the mortal expression of lesser gods. So instead I wonder what could added or even just highlighted more clearly to make Exigents feel like a splat of their own rather than just a toolbox to make the exalt of expressly the purview you need or for homebrewing Alchemicals and Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:32:01-07:00","id":1129360,"title":"","content":"I think it's easy to white-room the perfect Exigent for such-and-such a problem, but in practice it shouldn't be too much of an issue.<br /> <br /> I mean, say you're talking on a forum about which Exalt type is best at stabbing people, you could be like &quot;Hah, the Exigent of the God of stabbing people would kick your Invincible Sword Princess's ass!&quot; (Which they probably wouldn't, but they might be able to compete)<br /> <br /> But real games have lots of different problems, and most of them are not stabbing-related. What does the Exigent of the God of stabbing people do at a party?<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I frankly find God-Blooded more interesting from a fluff perspective, but I'm not worried about Exigents being a solution for every problem, because any particular Exigent is only going to be good at solving a small number of problems (or, perhaps, they can try and solve any problem, but only in a particular way, which means they're probably not going to be the best at it. If you're the Exigent of the God of revolutions, you'll be awesome at fomenting revolution, and you could certainly try dealing with social problems through revolution, but what if revolution isn't the best way to solve the nation's lack of doctors? So you're not going to be the perfect tool for every problem).<br /> <br /> I am worried about how the devs are going to write a book that helps you do homebrew, because I think that's actually really hard to do well (and, I'll admit, I think I'd find Exigent PCs a lot of hassle as an ST, because there's so much to approve), but I'm not worried about them being the perfect solution for every problem.<br /> <br /> Mostly, Exigents just sound like a lot of work to me. They* could, potentially, be awesome. I think they're also really useful for the ST, if you have a great idea for a really bizarre or unique NPC who wouldn't fit as anything else.<br /> I just can dread a player coming along with a really unbalanced Exigent idea they've based on the guidelines and hassling me to approve it all. And they might have a good fluff idea, but then we'd have to go and argue over every single homebrew charm... with some players, it'd be great, with others it could be a giant hassle, and it's not like I can tell my players that some of them can play Exigents and some of them can't. That's just mean.<br /> <br /> *I don't mean Exigents as a whole might be awesome, I mean any specific Exigent might be awesome. I think Exigents will be really variable, not something you could judge the coolness of as a whole, but it really gives players the potential to come up with something extremely interesting. Or something awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-15-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:32:16-07:00","id":1129361,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of what you're seeing is a symptom of us being stuck with only the corebook.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-15-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:37:39-07:00","id":1129362,"title":"","content":"That's probably true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:39:22-07:00","id":1129363,"title":"","content":"Also, I think god blooded as mini-exalts is one of the worst things that ever happened to the gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:40:26-07:00","id":1129364,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I see what you mean, but I think that's more about how people on the forums are home-brewing them than anything inherent in their concept.<br /> <br /> There is definitely a temptation to tailor an exigent to a situation, especially since exigents seem to be often created specifically to address some problem. However what we know of exigents is that they're empowered by individual gods with themes relevant to that god.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure that it makes sense for an exigent to be tailored to any specific problem. Consider that a god's powers are a reflection of their place and purpose. A god of the field is gonna have field powers, a god of the river is gonna have river powers etc. Now to me, if they're encountering something that they can't deal with on their own and they feel it's worth spending some of themselves to create an exigent, that doesn't seem like it would be directly related to their power set. If the god can solve the problem with a pure application of their powers, what need have they of the exigent? <br /> <br /> I dunno, I'm gonna reserve final judgement until we actually have the exigents book in hand (hopefully after lunars)<br /> <br /> As for powered up god bloods, they seem to me to have a very different place in the setting. An exigent may cost a good chunk of the God's power to create, if not kill them outright. Such a sacrifice is very different animal than &quot;I slept with a mortal. It was awesome. Oh hey, super-powerful offspring I can maybe sorta guide/teach that have all my powers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:48:02-07:00","id":1129368,"title":"","content":"I think probably it will also help to have a bunch of examples based on interesting gods, that aren't just &quot;the god of punching really hard&quot; but rather have a set of rather complicated themes and conceptual space.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T12:56:23-07:00","id":1129370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129363#post1129363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think god blooded as mini-exalts is one of the worst things that ever happened to the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see where there was room to merge the two, if your father is the god of the forest you are god blooded and nine times out of ten that just means you might have green hair, but that tenth child under certain circumstances might be GOD BLOODED and invested with a fragment of their parents power to fulfill some greater purpose. You could drop the idea that every god blooded is a mini exalt, while still having some reach that Exigent power level with that more narratively meaty theme of being the child of a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:23:32-07:00","id":1129389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129370#post1129370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I see where there was room to merge the two, if your father is the god of the forest you are god blooded and nine times out of ten that just means you might have green hair, but that tenth child under certain circumstances might be GOD BLOODED and invested with a fragment of their parents power to fulfill some greater purpose. You could drop the idea that every god blooded is a mini exalt, while still having some reach that Exigent power level with that more narratively meaty theme of being the child of a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's room but in a practical sense the green haired child got pushed out by their essence wielding sibling 9 times out of 10. Most of the time I saw them come up in threads it was about how the right package of Merits and Flaws could make them the a viable alternative to Dragon-Blooded while we've gone through a few forum transitions since then you can probably still find some on RPGnet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-15-2017, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:37:40-07:00","id":1129397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129389#post1129389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's room but in a practical sense the green haired child got pushed out by their essence wielding sibling 9 times out of 10. Most of the time I saw them come up in threads it was about how the right package of Merits and Flaws could make them the a viable alternative to Dragon-Blooded you can probably still find some on RPGnet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that God Blooded were used as an end run around thematic limitations DB in the previous edition, but it seems to me now that Exigents are even worse in this regard because the range of their power up to rivaling solars makes them candidates to make end runs around the limitations of EVERY type of exalt.<br /> <br /> To your point of mundane god blooded being pushed out by their empowered siblings, i'm not sure I see the difference between that and how every other exalt works. For every person who stands up to a greedy landowner and exalts as a Zenith multitudes more try the same thing, get run through with a sword, burried in a shallow grave, and we never hear about them. You are always going to be focused on the exceptions whether they be PCs or NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T13:55:40-07:00","id":1129409,"title":"","content":"Kind of hard to get a handle on. What's &quot;too often&quot; or &quot;disproportionately&quot; here? What's an example / cutoff of what you'd call being &quot;perfectly endowed with the godly power to exactly fit the situation as it arises&quot;?<br /> <br /> With them, I actually kind of feel more, now, like you won't see a lot of them for a couple reasons<br /> <br /> 1) Mechanical complexity, obviously. People will want to make characters with similar depth / progression frequency and granularity to existing characters, and Exalted 3 Charms seem kind of complex balanced (in the sense of being built to work well and be balanced in the system when tested, but not prioritising it really clearly be so obvious why that's the case - this is something the devs actually said!). So that means writing and testing a lot of mechanics per player Exigent.<br /> <br /> 2) Implicit setting restrictions. They're the &quot;Chosen of Whatever You Want&quot;, but at the same time there's a strong vibe (and probably actual setting rule!) that you shouldn't be making Exigents who are so broad and strong that the risk overshadowing any of the classic five. <br /> <br /> So this is the whole kind of &quot;Exigents should be a kind of one dimensional, one trick weird witch who bites it outside their comfort zone and doesn't have too much effect on the overall world&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> For most people, it seems like that would have less appeal compared to just picking up a game that's totally built around playing the &quot;Chosen of Whatever You Want&quot;, like Godbound or even Scion, and doesn't labour under those restrictions. (Like, for example, if you want to play this mythic demigod ur-ranger figure, then if you pick up a game like Godbound then you can create a character with words of Fertility, Beasts, Bow, and then not really worry too much after that about if your character is overshadowing any extant character types, or too strong for what level his type is allowed, or anything like that.)<br /> <br /> ... But then it's like &gt;two years since I heard about them and I still really don't know too much about their story or how they will work! So.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T14:15:09-07:00","id":1129424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129397#post1129397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that God Blooded were used as an end run around thematic limitations DB in the previous edition, but it seems to me now that Exigents are even worse in this regard because the range of their power up to rivaling solars makes them candidates to make end runs around the limitations of EVERY type of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div> The people in question weren't doing it to play them though, hell if they'd done that I'd have wished them godspeed. It was how they could fuck out a conquering army.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T14:37:16-07:00","id":1129437,"title":"","content":"What exactly are you worried about in the context of being a 'Generic Catch-all' here? I can't really understand it.<br /> <br /> Are you complaining about it as a GM dealing with players and their choice of PC? Are you worried about people showing up to campaigns set in the West as 'The Exigent of the God of Sailing' and the GM being unable to deal with that? While that may be reasonable I think unless you're just making your Exigent jacked to the gills even an Exigent of the God of Sailing is going to have times in the West where they aren't Sailing.<br /> <br /> Are you complaining about it as a Player and what the GM is using? Like are you worried that GMs are going to show up with 'The Exigent of Fighting on Cliffs while wielding a Spear' as your PC travels up a cliff? That probably isn't exactly accurate for what Exigents should do, and such an Exigent definitely should be on the weaker side for being so specific. It seems that Exigents as a whole are more looking for either 'Unique but maybe not powerful Gods' like Ten Sheaves, or something like 'Powerful and generally applicable', something like the Exigent of Cattle and Southern War. I'd imagine an ST is more likely to set you up against the second one then some kind of generic 'Exigent used specifically as a one off challenge', particularly if they're following the book talking about how Exigence is rare and difficult to use. I don't know why you would make an Exigent as an antagonist if you aren't going to give them spotlight; seems a lot of effort for a one-off enemy, all things considered.<br /> <br /> Or are you complaining about Players abusing Exigence not through their choice of character but rather their solutions to problems? Like are you worried that, upon being faced with a locked door in a campaign, rather then having the Night pick it or whatever they go 'Let's go find the Exigent of Lockpicking to pick the lock for us'. For a worry like this, I'm not sure how valid it is, because a player willingly going 'okay I'm going to give up spotlight to let an NPC succeed rather then risk failing' isn't a player I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I now see you asked this same question in the ask the devs thread right before making this topic. I can tell this topic is really worrying you in some respects so I'm interested in understanding what you're worried about here, because it seems like TDO's response didn't make you feel reassured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 08-15-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T15:36:49-07:00","id":1129460,"title":"","content":"I am curious how the power of the sponsor effects the power of the Exalt. Since the range of power seems to be from below to the power of the Terrestrial Exalted to below the power of the Celestial Exalted, it suggests that the range will depend on the Essence of the sponsor. <br /> <br /> I think that creating an Exalt should require the sacrifice of one permanent Willpower from both the sponsor and recipient and the maximum permanent Essence of the Exalt should not equal the maximum permanent Essence of their sponsor. I also think that there should also be a chance for the sponsor to be destroyed by the process, requiring an Essence roll to avoid destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T16:21:53-07:00","id":1129473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129437#post1129437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly are you worried about in the context of being a 'Generic Catch-all' here? I can't really understand it.<br /> <br /> Are you complaining about it as a GM dealing with players and their choice of PC? Are you worried about people showing up to campaigns set in the West as 'The Exigent of the God of Sailing' and the GM being unable to deal with that? While that may be reasonable I think unless you're just making your Exigent jacked to the gills even an Exigent of the God of Sailing is going to have times in the West where they aren't Sailing.<br /> <br /> Are you complaining about it as a Player and what the GM is using? Like are you worried that GMs are going to show up with 'The Exigent of Fighting on Cliffs while wielding a Spear' as your PC travels up a cliff? That probably isn't exactly accurate for what Exigents should do, and such an Exigent definitely should be on the weaker side for being so specific. It seems that Exigents as a whole are more looking for either 'Unique but maybe not powerful Gods' like Ten Sheaves, or something like 'Powerful and generally applicable', something like the Exigent of Cattle and Southern War. I'd imagine an ST is more likely to set you up against the second one then some kind of generic 'Exigent used specifically as a one off challenge', particularly if they're following the book talking about how Exigence is rare and difficult to use. I don't know why you would make an Exigent as an antagonist if you aren't going to give them spotlight; seems a lot of effort for a one-off enemy, all things considered.<br /> <br /> Or are you complaining about Players abusing Exigence not through their choice of character but rather their solutions to problems? Like are you worried that, upon being faced with a locked door in a campaign, rather then having the Night pick it or whatever they go 'Let's go find the Exigent of Lockpicking to pick the lock for us'. For a worry like this, I'm not sure how valid it is, because a player willingly going 'okay I'm going to give up spotlight to let an NPC succeed rather then risk failing' isn't a player I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I now see you asked this same question in the ask the devs thread right before making this topic. I can tell this topic is really worrying you in some respects so I'm interested in understanding what you're worried about here, because it seems like TDO's response didn't make you feel reassured.</div> </div> </div> </div>I posted in the ask devs thread...and then immediately thought &quot;this should be its own thread&quot; lol. Vance's answer wasn't the catalyst of me posting here.<br /> <br /> In regards to what concerns me more. I do see situation where exigents as PC characters could cover a purview that is too narratively empowering...but really Solars already do that.<br /> <br /> My bigger concern is the other view you suggested as a PC facing the GMs Exigents. Now the Exigent of fighting on cliffs with spears is hyperbole, but I do think there is the potential of a easy and boring route for a GM to throw a war god exigent every time he needs a military threat, a trade god exigent ever time he needs to oppose you in a negotiation, or a exigent of a god of artifice to explain away first age shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T16:30:52-07:00","id":1129477,"title":"","content":"I think so long as the Exigent is designed to be reasonable, fit the thematic of the God it came from, and creates an interesting challenge, then it wouldn't really be that big of a deal would it? In this case what would the GM have replaced the Exigent with it didn't exist? Probably an Outcaste Dragonblooded, right? That could get boring if you have nothing but Outcaste DBs as far as you can see, at least the Exigent solution leads you to having to differentiate them- if not in mechanics, then at least in appearance-.<br /> <br /> I doubt many GMs will just willy-nilly throw Exigents whenever the party needs competition, because they take a lot of work to make one, and if you're using the same generic Exigent over and over and just slapping a different template on it, then really it's no different from someone just using a DB in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T16:48:03-07:00","id":1129483,"title":"","content":"I think that an independent talon of Lookshy mercenaries (assisted by a scale of special forces and a scale of support staff) would be an adequate alternative to random Outcaste DB. It would require intelligent strategy to deal with and could be the focus of a few game sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T17:03:26-07:00","id":1129486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all#post1129350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to what concerns me more. I do see situation where exigents as PC characters could cover a purview that is too narratively empowering...but really Solars already do that.<br /> <br /> My bigger concern is the other view you suggested as a PC facing the GMs Exigents. Now the Exigent of fighting on cliffs with spears is hyperbole, but I do think there is the potential of a easy and boring route for a GM to throw a war god exigent every time he needs a military threat, a trade god exigent ever time he needs to oppose you in a negotiation, or a exigent of a god of artifice to explain away first age shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, remember that all Exalted can solve any problem. You aren't going to come across a problem that can't be &quot;solved&quot; by a Solar, or a Lunar or anyone else. If the ST essentially decides that the &quot;problem&quot; for his campaign is defeating the Mask of Winters and freeing Thorns, any Exalted type that the players are playing will be able to succeed. The difference will be in the process of how they succeed. Whether one player is playing a Solar or a Sidereal or an Exigent of Masque of Repose isn't going to change their ability to &quot;solve&quot; the problem, just how they go about doing so.<br /> <br /> The same thing is true of Exalted in the ST's hands. If the ST wants to have a trading organization led by an Exalt as a challenge to the players, he <i>could</i> have an Exigent of the goddess of money. Or he could have the leader be a Solar, Abyssal, Lunar or any other Exalt. Having Exigents just gives the ST one more &quot;tool in the toolbox&quot; to pull out. But the thing worth remembering is that 1) creating a new Exigent is a lot of work, and 2) the Exigent isn't going to be any more powerful than a Solar Exalt. So if the ST just wanted the &quot;strongest Exalt&quot; he can get, then he could have just stuck with the Solar to begin with.<br /> <br /> So I don't think there's much fear of Exigents unbalancing the game, or being used too often by players or STs. The biggest problem with them that I can foresee is players and ST's poorly balancing custom Charms and breaking the game wide open. Of course, I've seen the same thing happen with players making Solar Charms (and even with some of the published authors making Charms that ruined the game). Still though, Exigents are a full splat that encourages that sort of creativity and I suspect that you'll end up seeing a lot of complaints like, &quot;Fuck Exigents! My player made this bullshit Charm, and I didn't have enough system mastery to recognize the flaws, agreed to let him play it and wrecked the game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T17:06:49-07:00","id":1129488,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's why they make me nervous. On the other hand, I'd also be worried about being too strict, and killing players' creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T17:56:23-07:00","id":1129511,"title":"","content":"The thing is if you ever make a broken charm, generally you and your players both should be able to recognize it's doing bad things to the game and counteract it. Game Balance is a table thing, not a Book thing, at least in 3E; what's balanced for one table is broken for another, and so on. Exigents are, at both their best and worst, simply the detail of custom charms writ large, both for STs and Players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:24:50-07:00","id":1129537,"title":"","content":"I will defer the OP to the first rule of Exalted: The storyteller is free to change anything they don't like. Just because it was published in the Core Rulebook doesn't mean that you have to use it. If the Storyteller doesn't like it, they don't have to use it or even allow it. I know some players might not like it if you made such a change but if you feel uncomfortable using Exigents in your game then don't use them. It's just another option. Same with God-Blooded characters, you don't have to use them. I've only ever used God-Blooded characters as NPCs in my own games, none of my players ever expressed any interest in playing such a character. So far I've used Exigents as NPC builds to create more interesting game situations. You don't have to put them on the table as player options. It all depends on what you want for your series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6162-raven79","name":"Raven79","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6162_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:57:08-07:00","id":1129553,"title":"","content":"I'm also worried about Exigent being too good an option too.<br /> why go with the god-blooded of a forest god with 1-3 charms to make things grow when you can get an full fledged exigent?<br /> i mean shur it's a diference in &quot;allies&quot; points but if teh ST is going to spend time on characters why spend time on the lesser end of teh scale when engaging with high powered splats like solars.<br /> Now my ST fixed that problem by making teh PCs design ther allies and the NPCs we met were mostly statless unless they were going to take on important roll","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13802-black-silver-fox","name":"Black Silver Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:15:23-07:00","id":1129565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Silver Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129553#post1129553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also worried about Exigent being too good an option too.<br /> why go with the god-blooded of a forest god with 1-3 charms to make things grow when you can get an full fledged exigent?<br /> i mean shur it's a diference in &quot;allies&quot; points but if teh ST is going to spend time on characters why spend time on the lesser end of teh scale when engaging with high powered splats like solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not pick a Wood Aspect terrestrial sorcerer? Most any niche you could imagine an Exigent filling a game is a niche another Exalt could fill just as well (and would have been fulfilling if Exigents didn't exist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:31:47-07:00","id":1129570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Silver Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129553#post1129553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why go with the god-blooded of a forest god with 1-3 charms to make things grow when you can get an full fledged exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are members of this community who are quite vocal over repeatedly choosing to play Terrestrials or even mortals over Solars in their games.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf somebody has a general image of something associated with forests, and wants to go for the most heavily equipped option available for that, they might go for an Exigent.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf somebody wants to play a forest god-blood specifically, then they will.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe game is so heavily riddled with counter examples, and yet we keep needing to go through this song and dance of &quot;if this thing doesn't have some kind of optimised option, why would <i>anybody</i>, out of <b>all the roleplayers</b>, want to play them?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:45:07-07:00","id":1129627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129360#post1129360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Exigent of the God of stabbing people do at a party?</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul-honing Meditation: With a minute's pause and meditation, the Exigent restores focus and sharpness to their soul that they will turn to use shortly. They gain a specialty in any one skill for a scene. This is a non-charm die.<br /> <br /> Sheathed Blade, Still Tongue: The Exalt disappears into the crowd at a social occasion. They gain 2 dice to all attempts to remain unnoticed as long as they do not directly engage in social interaction with their targets; polite mingling with the crowd, asking for a drink, or Reading Intentions from afar do not affect this.<br /> <br /> Heart-Piercing Barb: The Exigent's words, as with all his actions, are direct and felt keenly. When attempting an Inspire action, all targets treat it as though it were playing off a Minor Intimacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:29:04-07:00","id":1129656,"title":"","content":"Wine Whets the Blade: When targeting an entity who shares food or drink with the Exalt, the target gains a Major Intimacy towards the Exalt.<br /> <br /> Lethal Cutlery Exercise: The Exalt treats cutlery as light weapons until the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Sublime Cutlery Meditation: The Exalt treats cutlery as light artifact weapons until the end of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:44:48-07:00","id":1129662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129360#post1129360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But real games have lots of different problems, and most of them are not stabbing-related. What does the Exigent of the God of stabbing people do at a party?</div> </div> </div> </div>Party tricks of course.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WBQTxb1jf14\" data-code=\"WBQTxb1jf14\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/WBQTxb1jf14/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:02:01-07:00","id":1129724,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to see my suggestion has inspired people! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Silver Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129553#post1129553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also worried about Exigent being too good an option too.<br /> why go with the god-blooded of a forest god with 1-3 charms to make things grow when you can get an full fledged exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why play the god-blooded of a forest when you can play a Solar? Or a Lunar? Or a Dragon-blood?<br /> <br /> I think if someone's playing a god-blooded with 1-3 charms, then either it's a very low-powered game, or they're deliberately playing something weak as a challenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bThere are members of this community who are quite vocal over repeatedly choosing to play Terrestrials or even mortals over Solars in their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played a ghost-blood in a Solar game for a few sessions, but the Solars bullied me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I also played a mortal in a Solar game. It was loads of fun.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing a Solar in said Solar game, but I'll probably retire him and play a DB when that book comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Silver Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now my ST fixed that problem by making teh PCs design ther allies and the NPCs we met were mostly statless unless they were going to take on important roll</div> </div> </div> </div>Shhhhh!<br /> Don't let the players know about the unstatted NPCs. It's a secret!<br /> (I tend to stat up the key antagonists of a game, but most NPCs get statted on the fly, with whatever stats I feel are reasonable. Works fine. The key is to just not go overboard and give them too much.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:37:03-07:00","id":1129730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Silver Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129553#post1129553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why go with the god-blooded of a forest god with 1-3 charms to make things grow when you can get an full fledged exigent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming god blooded still access their parent's charms like they did in last edition (ignoring Half-Caste here for everyone's collective sanity).<br /> <br /> Spirit charms are very good at letting you avoid direct confrontation in a way that's unlikely to be reflected by the charmset of a fully-fledged Exigent with Hurry Home and Dematerialize as two examples of this that we know have survived to 3rd edition relatively unchanged from previous editions. A god blooded thief with those two charms is invisible and can walk through walls and provided they have 10 motes left can respond to getting caught by teleporting away, there's Night Caste Solars who would be understandably jealous of that!<br /> <br /> Why am I so sure Exigents won't be able to do that? Quite simply, these are charms that just shouldn't go at the start of charm trees and the god blooded only gets to skip to the end like that because they don't possess the ability to refine it.<br /> <br /> But yes, this isn't an isolated example, if I'm not limiting myself to the 3rd edition corebook I can keep finding ways a minor spirit or god blooded could be a dangerous nuisance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:40:44-07:00","id":1129808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129724#post1129724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why play the god-blooded of a forest when you can play a Solar? Or a Lunar? Or a Dragon-blood?</div> </div> </div> </div> Better yet why compromise? The god blooded can be any of those.<br /> <br /> Also, while it feels like a lifetime ago <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vqs4F-V7tvQ&amp;t=1h03m00s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is what where the big podcast covered god blooded.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:44:53-07:00","id":1129812,"title":"","content":"True. It's a bit awkward to do mechanically* (though not so much if you play an Eclipse), but if you just want the fluff of having green hair and barky skin, and some appropriate specialties, no problem.<br /> <br /> *Personally, as ST, I'd probably work with the players to create some merits that give them some minor but appropriate powers. But there's not any actual rules for it currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:03:47-07:00","id":1129815,"title":"","content":"Yes but there's not actual rules for Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, God Blooded or Exigents currently either.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:14:29-07:00","id":1129822,"title":"","content":"A fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T00:56:19-07:00","id":1130171,"title":"","content":"I see Exigents role primarily as plot devices. For example:<br /> <br /> - Exalted of God X wanders into the PCs lives, causes trouble or enlists their help in the pursuit of a goal, then fades into the background. <br /> <br /> - The PCs are too specialised in Y, so along comes an exigent who is immune to Y and forces the PCs to adapt and broaden.<br /> <br /> - antagonist Z turns out to be a secret Exigent - surprise!<br /> <br /> While I'm always interested in seeing what a new player option looks like, my expectations re that a group of Exigents would be like a D&amp;D group of entirely chaotic alignments. They all have their own goals and agendas and their divine (parent?) will have shit that needs doing the PCs can't ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T06:45:27-07:00","id":1130230,"title":"","content":"I think that Exigents should be more narrowly defined than Celestial and Terrestrial Exalted. I would suggest that their Charm Trees should have a maximum of nine Charms per Ability or fifteen Charms per Attribute. Of course, they could develop Martial Arts Charms without limitation, and the limitation would not prevent stackable Charms.<br /> <br /> I would suggest that entities with an Essence 5-7 could create Exigents with the capabilities of a Terrestrial Exalted in Martial Arts and Sorcerey and entities with Essence 8-10 could create entities with the capabilities of a Celestial Exalted in Martial Arts and Sorcery. I wonder, could a powerful Elemental create Exigents, or is it restricted to Gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:20:54-07:00","id":1130236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130230#post1130230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that entities with an Essence 5-7 could create Exigents with the capabilities of a Terrestrial Exalted in Martial Arts and Sorcerey and entities with Essence 8-10 could create entities with the capabilities of a Celestial Exalted in Martial Arts and Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hesitant to propose mechanical systematizations before the hardback comes out, but I'm pretty sure this is looking at the process the wrong way. Keep in mind that the Exigent we've seen the most of, Strawmaiden Janest, was Exalted by a field guardian -- an incredibly minor god with a default essence of <i>1</i>.<br /> <br /> The point of the Exigents is that they can surpass that which endowed them -- that's why they were made in the first place. Insofar as we've seen a connection between the power of the god in question and the results of their work, it's that more powerful gods are capable of surviving a process which regularly kills little gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder, could a powerful Elemental create Exigents, or is it restricted to Gods? </div> </div> </div>It's gods-only, not any other kind of spirit or being; at least, that's what Morke said when asked, and I haven't seen any indication that the new devs are likely to change this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":3907,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","user":"Aretii","date":", whoops 08-17-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:34:15-07:00","id":1130247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129488#post1129488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's why they make me nervous. On the other hand, I'd also be worried about being too strict, and killing players' creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you trust them to make a custom martial art style? because I consider that a fairly appropriate comparison. Trading in the sheer effectiveness of a Solar combat tree for something more narrow and esoteric in function. My experience was that while there was scope for bad mechanical interaction it was rare to see anything that was terrible in and of itself on paper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T07:52:06-07:00","id":1130260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129730#post1129730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming god blooded still access their parent's charms like they did in last edition\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Why assume that? The old devs said that wasn't going to be how it worked, and while the new devs haven't spoken on the matter (that I recall!), why would they reverse that decision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T08:47:42-07:00","id":1130285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130260#post1130260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why assume that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because that's my only frame of reference for a god blooded with charms and how I suspect a lot of people are going to handle them until they get official coverage. I also feel comfortable predicting they're going to retain the ability to enter an immaterial state because it's one of their major distinguishing features from Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T08:57:56-07:00","id":1130293,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the only issue I see with Exigents is the fact they're basically legitimized homebrew. And frankly, homebrew making or breaking your game is something you'll hear about from any number of stories, good and bad. At that point, it's a question of how well your GM and players handle things and dealing with what everyone wants to have fun with.<br /> <br /> Anything you can do with a godblood, you can do with an Exigent, but anything you can do with an Exigent, you can do with a Solar/DB/Lunar/Whatever You Want. I think Exigents open up easier paths to getting what you thematically want, but they're just homebrew generated content with a coat of legitimacy paint. They're not going to break the game any more than Nocturnals or Terrifying Argent Witches or Infernals or whatever, because when it comes down to it, what something does to &quot;the line&quot; is secondary to what your table decides on. So if you and your players are having fun, there's no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:02:48-07:00","id":1130298,"title":"","content":"I would rather that there was standardization though, to prevent the normal arguments associated with homebrewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:35:46-07:00","id":1130312,"title":"","content":"It seems certain that there will be standards and guidelines provided in the Exigents book for how not to break the game by unleashing Invincible Sword Princess and her four identical siblings, but &quot;power level&quot; is really contextual and hard to quantify unless everyone's powers are super generic, at which point the game fails to deliver on its promise (e.g. how in 2E Lunar Charms seemed a lot like someone had gone through the Solar Charmset and said &quot;these, but less efficient for the magnitude of the effect&quot;). My point was just that &quot;Essence rating of the god in question&quot; doesn't seem likely to be extremely relevant to the power of the Exigent; it felt to me implied in the fluff from the 3E core that the Exigence, the portion of the Unconquered Sun's power that he made available for this purpose, does most of the work, since the god's own Essence is referred to as &quot;catalyzing&quot; the process.<br /> <br /> Also, the Terrestrial-Celestial divide seems like less of a Giant Thing that will be mechanically enforced. Many 2E Dragonblooded Charms <i>literally</i> have riders saying something like &quot;but Celestial Charms beat this automatically if there's a contest,&quot; as part of Ye Grand Plan To Make DBs Seem Terrible And Sucky In Their Own Book. That's gone in 3E; the differences between Terrestrials and Celestials, in terms of how the one is generally weaker than the other, is in the Charm pool (the ways in which Dragonblooded Essence expresses itself) and the weaker Excellency, but that same difference also causes DBs to be contextually stronger (they're repeatedly called out in the core as masters of Evocations second only to the Solars, and in some respects their peer).<br /> <br /> There will always be arguments about homebrewing, but I worry that systematizing it too much leads to the issue one sees in superhero games, where powers are generic things to be point-bought and then refluffed, but fundamentally the same thing underneath the surface. Rejecting that route makes it harder on everyone to make good material, but I think leads to better games and stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:21:10-07:00","id":1130363,"title":"","content":"But there are noticeable differences between Terrestrial and Celestial Exalted when it comes to Martial Arts and Sorcery (and presumably Necromancy). Terrestrial Exalted are weaker than Celestial Exalted when using Martial Arts Charms that are not tailored for their use and cannot practice Celestial Sorcery. Since Exigents vary in power from Terrestrial Exalted to Celestial Exalted, we would expect similar divisions (though the dividing line might be patron Essence 5- equals Terrestrial Exalted equivalent while patron Essence 6+ equals Celestial Exalted equivalent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:14:46-07:00","id":1130393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1129570#post1129570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf somebody wants to play a forest god-blood specifically, then they will.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe game is so heavily riddled with counter examples, and yet we keep needing to go through this song and dance of &amp;quot;if this thing doesn't have some kind of optimised option, why would <i>anybody</i>, out of <b>all the roleplayers</b>, want to play them?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. In fact because the way Solars are supposed to work, barring a few notable exceptions, you can even make the argument that from a strictly mechanical point of view why make anything but a Solar with the proper merits/sorcery/charms/evocations ect. to fit whatever your concept is?<br /> <br /> But you can't really be a Solar who received his exaltation from his grandfather when he passed the legendary blade down to him, or be a Solar who has the power to ride waves like camels because their father was a surf god whom he is still beholden to, or be a Solar who is the little fish cogwheel in the machinations of his giant and much more powerful family.<br /> <br /> You might even not be a Solar because you don't want to be a force of nature capable of shaking the pillars of heaven, but just want to be a smaller hero without the temptation to go bigger.<br /> <br /> <br /> But if you're looking at those and feeling that the list of things it's hard to do with a Solar is limited, that's because it's supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:17:41-07:00","id":1130395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130298#post1130298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather that there was standardization though, to prevent the normal arguments associated with homebrewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, me too. A certain amount of standardisation is what I want from the book, though obviously it's going to be quite hard for the writers to do that while still allowing homebrewability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you trust them to make a custom martial art style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmmmmmmm...<br /> Maybe 1 or 2 of them.<br /> I think I'd trust most of them (not all of them*) to do it, with help from others. Which for one martial arts style, I reckon would be fine, but if they're writing 30+ charms, other players might be less interested in it. But it'd probably okay.<br /> Until I have to approve 30+ charms. At least an MA is only about 9, in a very definite theme, with related mechanics.<br /> <br /> *This is the issue. I can't really say &quot;You guys can play an Exigent, but that guy can't.&quot; I mean, some players wouldn't mind: if I said &quot;Iozz-Sothoth, you're a fluff man not a mechanics man, you can play an Exigent if you've got a cool concept, but only if someone else writes the rules for you&quot;, I don't think Iozz-Sothoth would mind, because he doesn't care that much about mechanics anyway (and probably wouldn't want to write them up, just come up with vague ideas), but others might mind. And if I say &quot;Owen can play Exigents because he comes up with really cool ideas for bizarre but not overpowered characters, like when he wanted to play a magic sword that controls the guy wielding it, and I know he doesn't care if the charms are powerful or not, but the power-gamers in the group can't because they'll have concepts designed for getting max power.**&quot;<br /> <br /> **I include myself in this group. I would not let myself play an Exigent.<br /> <br /> As Aya Tari says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the normal arguments associated with homebrewing </div> </div> </div>This is actually one of the things I dislike most about running Exalted (well, any games, but with Rogue Trader that I'm running now, it's not really something that's come up). Arguing with players about what their homebrew stuff should do. I found adjudicating sorcerous workings (which are, essentially, homebrew with guidelines, so a little similar to what Exigents are likely to be) quite irritating (the absolute worst thing is when the player eventually convinces me to let them do the working they want, but I nerf it in various ways so it's not too powerful, and they grumble that it's too weak, and then other players complain that I've let that player have something really overpowered and it's so unfair, grumble, grumble).<br /> <br /> And Exigents seem like the same thing, but far, far more.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not saying that Exigents are bad for the game. For some people, they might be really fun. It's easy enough for me to say &quot;In my game, no-one can play Exigents&quot; (especially as I'm only playing right now, I probably won't run Exalted again for a couple of years.)<br /> I'm just pointing out potential problems, which I hope the writers can find ways to avoid. For example, reducing the amount of mechanical work that players/STs have to do is a key thing I'd like from the book, as is making it easy to ensure charms aren't overpowered***.<br /> <br /> ***Them being less powerful than Solars is really helpful, because any charm that's similar to a Solar charm just needs to be less powerful in some way than the Solar equivalent, and then you know it's okay. But I think it was once mentioned that they might be more powerful than Solars in very specialised areas, which worries me, as Solars are already very specialised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-17-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:29:41-07:00","id":1130403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130285#post1130285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also feel comfortable predicting they're going to retain the ability to enter an immaterial state because it's one of their major distinguishing features from Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it? I cannot recall it coming up much in discourse.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor that matter, there's the fact that gods didn't become immaterial with a Charm; it was their default state, and the Charm was needed to make them materialize.<br /> <br /> \u200bScroll of Heroes seems to imply that inheriting the Materialize Charm does not bestow a capability to become immaterial:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> God-Blooded have no normal use of Materialize. Yet, a God-Blood who possesses this Charm could use it to become material if she were somehow rendered immaterial. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:39:31-07:00","id":1130411,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's particularly genre-needed either. I can't remember any god-bloods in mythology having the power to turn intangible.<br /> <br /> Whereas, it's important that God-Bloodeds can potentially be really strong, because of Hercules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:57:13-07:00","id":1130422,"title":"","content":"hm...Exigence thoughts.<br /> <br /> I think Exigents have a single coherent theme that's not talked about a lot. Exigents are made to solve a problem, but outlive that solution. That's a space I don't think Exalted explores very much right now, in a 'whole splat' way.<br /> <br /> When I think of why I want the Exigent book, oddly, it's rarely for the Exigents. I kind of think of them as an Ex Miscellenia category, things that wouldn't make sense for an entire splat but still need a place in the world-a bloodline empowered to protect a lost land, the chosen of a river spirit to drive out the barbaric saxons, a supersolider project gone wrong, a champion of a gods lost flock, etc. And that's fine. What I'm more intreasted in is advice on how to model abillities and charms. How to homebrew better, I guess. Which does mean that Exigents are essentially homebrew, but homebrew with guiding principles, using developer advice, and so on. <br /> <br /> It'd also be nice, however, if your like me and you want to homebrew all sorts of weird stuff and need advice on how to mechanically model powers in general. Kinda like how I hope the Martial Arts book gives advice on how to design your own style, or the Sorcery book your own iniation, or Arms and your own evocations. Exigents are weird in that there, probably, isn't going to be a canon caste as universal as those (although I hope we get statlines for all the ones referenced in the core).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:11:57-07:00","id":1130426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130395#post1130395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the issue. I can't really say &quot;You guys can play an Exigent, but that guy can't.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is.<br /> The indication from Revana Quin's write-up in the core is that an Architect is a type of Exigent and I suspect the examples we're going to see in the eventual book (and hopefully beforehand!) are going to be of a similar nature so I think you're overestimating the level of mandatory homebrew.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130403#post1130403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it? I cannot recall it coming up much in discourse.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, much of the discourse I've seen is from pople who don't appear to play god blooded unless they're Exalts. There's certainly a general lack of understanding of what the spirit charmset is capable of in a PC's hands (it shows, oh my god does it show).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 08-17-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:24:18-07:00","id":1130435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scroll of Heroes seems to imply that inheriting the Materialize Charm does not bestow a capability to become immaterial:<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I went by the book that actually seems to know what its doing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Role of Glorious Divinity 1, page 143</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elementals, Eclipse Caste Solars, Moonshadow Caste Abyssals and God-Bloods learn a Charm called Dematerialize. </div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:28:26-07:00","id":1130437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130426#post1130426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is.<br /> The indication from Revana Quin's write-up in the core is that an Architect is a type of Exigent and I suspect the examples we're going to see in the eventual book (and hopefully beforehand!) are going to be of a similar nature so I think you're overestimating the level of mandatory homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought she was, and I liked the sound of that (and wanted to play an Architect: I really like her charms, and would like to see a lot more of that charmset!). I thought maybe they'd do charmsets for common god-types (like city gods, natural place gods, animal gods, etc... though in fact a lot of gods, especially Celestial ones, don't really fit into any particular category. And I guess city-gods are probably going to give out more similar powers than animal-gods, who are probably actually really different) but people told me that the devs said that in fact that's not it, and she is just an individual exalt because every single Exigent's powers are unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:41:12-07:00","id":1130446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130411#post1130411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas, it's important that God-Bloodeds can potentially be really strong, because of Hercules.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if this were Greek mythology I'd agree with you.<br /> <br /> In Exalted? I fully support that god-bloods should inherit some power from their progenitor. However, it seems to me that Greek heroes are better modeled by the exalted themselves and quite often solars in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:59:40-07:00","id":1130463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130437#post1130437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought she was, and I liked the sound of that (and wanted to play an Architect: I really like her charms, and would like to see a lot more of that charmset!). I thought maybe they'd do charmsets for common god-types (like city gods, natural place gods, animal gods, etc... though in fact a lot of gods, especially Celestial ones, don't really fit into any particular category. And I guess city-gods are probably going to give out more similar powers than animal-gods, who are probably actually really different) but people told me that the devs said that in fact that's not it, and she is just an individual exalt because every single Exigent's powers are unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, IIRC there aren't classes of exigent for god types (not all city gods create architects w/exigents for instance). I do hope we get a plethora of examples,though. That way, cribbing notes and ideas is easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:05:06-07:00","id":1130469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130446#post1130446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if this were Greek mythology I'd agree with you.<br /> <br /> In Exalted? I fully support that god-bloods should inherit some power from their progenitor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I don't see why it's important that this includes dematerialisation. For one thing, it's got nothing to do with that particular god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:16:14-07:00","id":1130473,"title":"","content":"The Exigent of the god of stabbing people sounds like too much fun not to build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:51:26-07:00","id":1130504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130469#post1130469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but I don't see why it's important that this includes dematerialisation. For one thing, it's got nothing to do with that particular god.</div> </div> </div> </div>No arguments from me. I don't think it makes sense at all for god bloods to be able to go immaterial or come back. I was merely stating that Greek mythology demigods fit better as full exalts than as God-Bloods in exalted<br /> <br /> /edit<br /> I should also state that the existence of exigence seems to diminish the god-bloods power level. If you can simply breed up an army of mortals who have similar powers to your own in scope and breadth why would you ever give up one or more dots of Essence or your very existence to grant exigence to somebody?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 08-17-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:05:51-07:00","id":1130523,"title":"","content":"In 1e, it was very expensive to dematerialize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:09:21-07:00","id":1130524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130504#post1130504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/edit<br /> I should also state that the existence of exigence seems to diminish the god-bloods power level. If you can simply breed up an army of mortals who have similar powers to your own in scope and breadth why would you ever give up one or more dots of Essence or your very existence to grant exigence to somebody?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The short answer?<br /> Exigents can exceed your power. Godblooded probably, typically, can't. I was personally under the impression that godblooded were normally <i>weaker</i> then their parents, while Exigents have the potential to be a lot stronger. Godblooded aren't uniform, granted, but still I assumed they are somewhere in Mist the Eternal Revolutionaires power level at their greatest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T15:10:37-07:00","id":1130526,"title":"","content":"Although, considering that the power level of God-Blooded was inconsistently applied, and at the upper level never really matched with depictions of the overall setting, a bit of consolidation might be in order regardless of the existence of Exigents.<br /> <br /> Mind, the question can still have answers.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor example, if Ten Sheaves had never gotten around to having a large number of children, it's not exactly an option for him when an army of Fair Folk is going to arrive tomorrow. The follow-up question of &quot;why didn't he have a large number of children&quot; could be answered by anything from him fearing that the presence of such a group would be highly disruptive to his domain, to simply not being very interested.<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, if you're a quite powerful god, I would say that the tone around Exigence (even if you happen to be strong enough for it to not destroy you) might imply that if you ever have to rely upon it, the other expressions of your power have already failed, whether they be your own divine strength, armies from nations dedicated to you, or children who have inherited some of that divine strength.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn top of that, there's the matter of how Exigents can have a decent amount of variation in their strength, regardless of the power of their patron. Assuming that Ten Sheaves does not deviate very much from the template of a harvest god that the core gave us, even in the best case scenario with Second Edition-style God-Blooded, the kinds of combat powers his children would have would not be very impressive against an army of Fair Folk. The Chosen of the Harvest seems to be endowed with something a bit more formidable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:00:47-07:00","id":1130597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130469#post1130469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I don't see why it's important that this includes dematerialisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Exalted &quot;child of two worlds&quot; is literally the god blooded thing, I mean look at the heritage power they've had that since Games of Divinity. If 3e decided to abandon that and use Scion as the basis for it's god blooded instead it'd probably be a bigger change to the setting than all the new exalt types combined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T17:41:33-07:00","id":1130616,"title":"","content":"I would not want Scion in Exalted, Demigod Scions are much too powerful for the world of Exalted (22 bonus successes on a roll would exceed the powers of even the Solar Exalted). The Hero level would be acceptable though (replacing Legend with Essence and Legend points with Essence motes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:14:20-07:00","id":1130922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130524#post1130524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The short answer?<br /> Exigents can exceed your power. Godblooded probably, typically, can't. I was personally under the impression that godblooded were normally <i>weaker</i> then their parents, while Exigents have the potential to be a lot stronger. Godblooded aren't uniform, granted, but still I assumed they are somewhere in Mist the Eternal Revolutionaires power level at their greatest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we actually have this officially? I realize that it sorta fits the recurring theme of being overcome by what you've created that exalted has going, but do we actually know that exigents are gonna be able to get more powerful than the god that spawn them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:20:42-07:00","id":1130924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130922#post1130922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we actually have this officially? I realize that it sorta fits the recurring theme of being overcome by what you've created that exalted has going, but do we actually know that exigents are gonna be able to get more powerful than the god that spawn them?</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have noted, Janest seems to be this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:21:14-07:00","id":1130925,"title":"","content":"Well, the exigent with the story, Strawmaiden Janest, is the exalt of a god of... a field. Maybe like a big field, or even several fields, but that's a pretty small terrestrial god. They're not god of fields generally. So I'd guess Essence 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> And I seriously doubt that the writers are going to say &quot;your character who was exalted by the god of the local river is not allowed to reach Essence 3 or higher.&quot;<br /> <br /> These are the kinds of gods that most Dragonblood are already more powerful than, and it'd be a shame of no-one wanted to play their Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:24:06-07:00","id":1130975,"title":"","content":"I don't want essence caps at all. The main thing a cap of 3 did for god blooded was make people not want to play them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:58:17-07:00","id":1130983,"title":"","content":"That's true. Even in the sort of games people played god-bloods in (generally low-essence stuff, like Raksha or Dragon Kings or maybe DBs), there wasn't much else that was restricted to Essence 3, IIRC.<br /> <br /> I had my PCs fight an Essence 4 god-blood near the end of my 3rd ed campaign. Her dad was Ahlat. I don't really see the problem there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T15:19:08-07:00","id":1130985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130922#post1130922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we actually have this officially? I realize that it sorta fits the recurring theme of being overcome by what you've created that exalted has going, but do we actually know that exigents are gonna be able to get more powerful than the god that spawn them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that &quot;get more powerful&quot; is the wrong way to approach this.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's more like... &quot;tier&quot; is still a term with faults, but to the extent that it is useful, it seems to me that the tier of a given Exigent does not need to depend upon the status of its patron. Perhaps Ahlat could make an Exigent who is about as powerful as a Liminal, while the god of a certain hill could produce somebody who is only slightly less powerful than a Solar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:18:27-07:00","id":1131003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all#post1129350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else feel that Exigents could become too much of a &quot;solution&quot; for every problem? Just in my personal experience and what I see on these forums it feels like they are showing up disproportionately as NPCs and Antagonists perfectly endowed with the godly power to exactly fit the situation as it arises. I think this stems from the way they have been presented, Exigents so far have no coherent theme as a splat the way Solars, DBs, Lunars, Sidereals, or Abyssals do, they just seem to be a toolbox to do anything but are missing those narrative walls which challenge players to work within them or break them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel differently. I loved the idea of the Exigents when they were presented. As an ST I feel it gives variety to the setting and provides me with other options than opponents A through E. In my games those Exalted by way of the Exigence are rare. There were a couple dozen when the Scarlet Empress was around, now there's not really that many more. So, the Exigents can't be used as a solution for every problem.<br /> <br /> Also in my games, most of the Exigents have outlived or passed on their power long after their original need necessitated their creation. Most of them are pursuing other objectives than protecting that one city or field or whatever it was their divine parent originally created them to do (particularly if the god was destroyed Exalting the mortal).<br /> <br /> I'm running a solo game for one of my children. Their character was Exalted by the goddess of the village well. The goddess along with the PC's village was destroyed. But he has fulfilled the task that was given him by his goddess. Now the PC is wrangling with the decision on what to do with his life. Whatever the PC decides to do, it won't be protecting his old village or serving the goddess who Exalted him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all#post1129350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think there never should have been Exigents in the first place, to me a much more interesting area to explore would have been beefed up god-blooded and a exploration of familial expectation, inheritance, and even apotheosis, but that seems like a moot thought at this point as the gameline has committed to Exigents as the mortal expression of lesser gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel there is plenty of room for Exigents and godblooded. All those things you mentioned are still entirely viable as godblooded stories and, as far as I understand what has been revealed regarding Exigents, would not be a good fit for Exigent stories. Godblooded are offspring and can pursue all types of stories. Exigents are soldiers like all other Exalted. They were created for a military purpose. At least, that's how I view Exigents based on the limited info on them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:26:53-07:00","id":1131773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1129350-are-exigents-yoo-much-of-a-generic-catch-all?p=1130437#post1130437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people told me that the devs said that in fact that's not it, and she is just an individual exalt because every single Exigent's powers are unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to imply that there's multiple Architects in the setting and she'd be recognised as one. <br /> <br /> She is however presented as a City Exigent rather than the Wu Jian Exalt because that's infinitely more usable to people. I like to imagine a full Architect charmset would posess a few obviously Wu Jian charms so there\u2019d be an easy path to adapt it to the service of another city so that even if someone wants to make an Exigent created by the City Father of Paragon that they've envisioned as ability based and more focused on imposing order because of the Perfect's long-term influence on the city, there's still going to be some familiar ideas there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}